now that bill has become a poly-expert he should be more efficient the next
time around...

playing nethack without polypiling usually takes time, however the fact is
that it is easier to polypile than to figure out how to survive various
attacks as a "weaker" character... a reasonable person would tend to
choose the easier route to glory since the scoreboard doesn't have flags
for martyrs, heroes and the like...

just saying no doesn't address the issue or solve the problem...

if a player legitimately chooses to polymorph wads of garbage he shouldn't
be given an "unfair advantage" (i.e. the generative aspects and so on).
being conscientious and clearly recognizing a "flawed" aspect of the game,
the abusers themselves have asked that it be amended to correct the "
advantage". that is more appropriate than ignoring it.

forget polymorph (for now) and consider the situation where engraving
"Elbereth" would prevent monsters from attacking you, would not scare them
away, would be semi-permanent in that you could use missile weapons without
worry (or an applied pick-axe). okay fine, you wouldn't use it but clearly
that aspect of the game would be flawed (ref. hack 1.0.2) and would need to
to be amended (not removed, drastically altered, etc.). "Elbereth" now
offers advantages and is also problematic and is difficult to abuse.
that's better than just saying no ...

it would seem from recent posts that amendments are afoot regarding
polypiling thus making discussion a somewhat moot point. in spite of all
its mystery frobozz has been reasonable in making the game not too hard
and not too easy. in this case the thing to do seems to be to wait and see
what's up with pl7 ...

